  "promotion_decision": "Not promoted. Translation/yaw tracking improves consistently, but effort and slip increase and fall events do not improve; tighter driver-contract and actual robot evidence remain required.",
  "failure_interpretation": "Fall threshold is30 degrees. Recovered has6 failures in 6 of 96 worlds; finetuned 7 in 7 of 96. Most occur during lateral commands. Two finetuned events occur 0.14/0.42 s after changing a moving command to stop; these are transition failures, not evidence that a settled stand is unstable.",
  "limitations": [
    "Three seeds of 32 worlds, each runs one 220 s continuous sequence; not 96 independent trials per command. No policy reset at command changes, but failures autoreset and are counted.",
    "Steady tracking averages use valid samples after 2 s warmup; failure events include transitions and invalid periods.",
    "Ranges across three seed-level means are descriptive, not confidence intervals. One extra failure does not by itself establish a statistically reliable increase in failure risk.",
    "Play settings retain startup mass/gain/bias/friction/COM and observation-noise variation, but exclude external pushes; no terrain, thermal, battery or hardware test.",
    "Torque-squared is a mechanical-effort proxy, not electrical energy. Contact slip is contacting-foot speed, not measured traction loss.",
    "Requested command limits are not achieved speeds or a validated operating envelope; original and finetuned policies remain separate from the shipped MixedGaitsJump policy."
